    "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR turns the existing job flow into a production-oriented marketplace state machine.\n\n### Lifecycle\n- adds `COMPLETION_REQUESTED`\n- worker accepts an `OPEN` job\n- assigned worker requests completion\n- requester confirms completion\n- escrow is released only after confirmation\n- direct cancellation is limited to unaccepted `OPEN` jobs\n\n### Safety and correctness\n- mutation paths use a pessimistic row lock to prevent two workers from accepting the same job concurrently\n- keeps optimistic `@Version` protection as a second line of defense\n- maps not-found / forbidden / conflict failures to 404 / 403 / 409\n- strengthens title, description and monetary validation\n- replaces manual `SecurityContextHolder` access with `@AuthenticationPrincipal`\n\n### Data model\n- adds lifecycle timestamps through Flyway `V2__job_lifecycle.sql`\n- adds an index for status + creation time\n- enriches `JobResponse` with actor IDs and lifecycle timestamps\n\n### Tests and documentation\n- adds focused unit tests for critical lifecycle invariants\n- documents state transitions and escrow rules in `docs/JOB_LIFECYCLE.md`\n\nCompatibility aliases `/take` and `/done` remain available while the canonical endpoints are `/accept` and `/confirm`.",
